        "note": "Theorem1.2 alone counted; subgroup exploration Theorem1.3 and harmonious-subgroup/geometry-of-numbers intermediate results remain uncounted shared core. For every K,k finite there are r0(K),C(K,k); applies to integer r≥r0 with Gr(3r)≤K Gr(r), counting dyadic relation scales n≥log2 r, not bounding the final scale itself. Named prerequisites: Breuillard–Green–Tao quantitative structure theorem as stated1.1, Pansu asymptotic Carnot metric, Minkowski second theorem, Lazard rational expansions, Tessera–Tointon Lemma4.4, Malcev lattice facts, Haar/BCH Jacobian compatibility and bounded-index Schreier generators5.3. All new lattice comparison, index sandwich, scaling and quotient-lifting core is printed. Editorial notice links a subsequent stronger Tessera/Tointon theorem, not an error correction; Remark1.3 records this and a later small-doubling improvement. Retain original small-tripling scope. No prior equivalent claim found in active metadata or ready lists. This is checked licensed published transcription; aggregate source-origin runtime qualification is explicitly pending.",
